// Golden vectors, determinism, resume, the stage entry point and schema 3
// of the biome stage (spec P1-04 sections 2, 3, 5 B6, 6 invariants 5 and 6,
// 7, 10.1 tests 7 and 9, 10.3 and 10.4; P1-03 3 and C7 for table
// `climate`; P1-00 sections 3, 9.2, 10.1 and 14 X1, X2; rule D10).
//
// The golden vectors in worldgen/tests/golden/p1-04-biomes.txt were
// generated by worldgen/tests/reference/p1_biomes_reference.py, the test
// writer's exact-integer reference written from the spec alone, with the
// input layers from the hydrology and climate references. Each case's
// inputs are recomputed by the earlier stages and compared first, so an
// upstream change shows as such. The items are then compared in step order,
// so a failure names the first step that diverges: the rain scale (seam
// biome_rain_scale), drainage height (seam height_above_drainage), slope,
// the jitter fields and tq, rq (the test's own B3), the B4 grid (seam
// biome_lookup per cell), the biome layer (seams biome_river_cells and
// biome_layer), the table hashes and the report values.
//
// P1-04 10.4's golden values for the world files are recorded by the
// validation specialist; these are the test writer's per-step vectors. The
// N >= 256 cases run in the suite "biomes-slow":
//   worldgen-tests -ts=biomes-slow --no-skip

